This document replaces GB 18030-2005 "Information technology - Chinese character encoding". Compared to GB 18030-2005, the main technical changes are as follows, apart from structural adjustments and editorial modifications:
The scope of applicability of this document (see Chapter 1) has been expanded.
Ten vertical punctuation marks and eight Chinese character components in the double-byte encoding area have been modified, and six repeated Chinese character components and nine repeated Chinese characters have been adjusted (see Appendix D, Appendix A of the 2005 edition).
Eighteen GB/T 13000 code positions in the four-byte encoding area were modified (see Appendix D, Appendix D of the 2005 edition);
The appendix "Additional Chinese characters and radicals/components" has been deleted, see Appendix 0 in the 2005 edition.
Level of implementation has been added " (see Appendix 9);
An appendix for reference, "General Normative Chinese Character Table; Code Position of Characters," see Appendix D.
