9.1 General Rules
This document specifies three implementation levels.
System software products that meet the corresponding implementation level should provide input and output functions for all characters within the scope of the corresponding implementation level.
9.2 Implementation Level 1
Implement level 1 support for the single-byte encoding section, the double-byte encoding section, and the four-byte encoding section of the CJK Unified Ideographs (i.e., 0x82358F33 to 0x82359636) and the CJK Unified Ideographs Extension A (i.e., 0x8139EE39 to 0x82358738).
Any product applicable to this document should meet the requirements of level 1.
Note: According to the software application requirements, level 1 can also choose any one or a combination of non-Chinese scripts listed in Table 3.
9.3 Implementation Level 2
Implementation level 2 includes implementation level 1.
In addition, level 2 implements the Chinese characters in the "General Chinese Character Set" that are not included in level 1.
The code position and character form of the Chinese characters included in the "General Standardized Chinese Characters Table" in this document are see Appendix D.
System software and supporting software should meet the requirements of level 2.
Note: System software and support software include but are not limited to operating systems, database management systems, middleware (information on software product classification is referenced in GB/T 36475).
9.4 Implementation Level 3
Implementation level 3 includes implementation level 2.
Furthermore, achieving level 3 includes all Chinese characters specified in this document and the Kangxi radicals listed in Table 3.
Products used for government services and public services should meet the requirements of level 3.
Note: The service industry and public service sector include but are not limited to the railway transportation industry, road transportation industry, water transportation industry, air transportation industry, multimodal transport and transport agency industry, postal industry, financial services, insurance industry, land and management industry, health care, state institutions, social security, etc. (Industry classification information is referred to in GB/T 4754).
