-fexternal-templates generates smaller code (limited to C++) by creating a copy of each template function only at the point of definition.
In order to successfully use this option, you must mark `#pragma implementation` (definition) or `#pragma interface` (declaration) in all files that use the template.
When compiling with `-fexternal-templates`, all template instantiations are considered external types. You must have the required instantiations appear in the implementation file.
This can be achieved through typedef, referencing each instance as needed.
Correspondingly, if the default option `-fno-exteznal-templates` is used during compilation, all template instances are explicitly set to built-in.
