He believes that developers today actually need more confidence than homebuyers, and introducing a "price protection agreement" is also a way to boost their confidence.
As for whether we can retain homebuyers, he said this depends on the influence of multiple factors such as regulatory policies and loan thresholds. As of now, it remains to be seen.
