The Chinese e-commerce industry has seen the emergence of "new variables." How can live streaming sales achieve "content as king"?
Xinhua News Agency
China News Agency, February 11th: Topic: The E-commerce Industry in China Emerges with "New Variables," How to Achieve "Content is King" in Live Streaming Sales?
Xia Bin, journalist of China New Finance
We entered the e-commerce field relatively late, but from the very beginning, we realized that content is very important if we want to stand out among the countless stores.
A "90s" girl from Guangdong, Fang Fang, is now operating a complement and health food store on Douyin E-commerce, helping a traditional offline store with a 30-year history to "bloom" online.
Imitating the style of old Hong Kong films, paired with classic Cantonese songs, opening @Fangfang's solo dining WeChat account, the exquisite videos are refreshing to the eyes.
At the recent Douyin E-commerce "Finding Companions · High-quality Content Sharing Special Session," Fang Fang, as a representative of high-quality creators, attended the event and gave a speech, sharing her experiences and insights in daily creation.
She said on the spot: "The carefully polished video has attracted a lot of attention from netizens. Many people are interested in the ingredients from my home and want to try making the food together, which has immediately opened up a sales channel."
The assistant will now provide the translation of the user's query from Chinese to English.
Fangfang, by relying on the soup-making video, has made more people love the "old Guangdong flavor." A single live stream can sell up to 300,000 pieces of nourishing ingredients, saving a family-owned shop that was on the brink of bankruptcy.
"No content, no e-commerce. As short video and live streaming e-commerce continue to develop, the requirements and standards for e-commerce content are entering a new phase."
In the early stages of live streaming e-commerce, live stream rooms often used low prices or discounts to attract users, and the price advantage seemed to be the only selling point at that time.
In recent years, there have been both phenomenon-level influencers such as Liu Fenhong and Dongfang Zhenxuan, as well as many niche influencers and merchants who are not widely known to the general public. They enhance their long-term operational benefits by consistently creating high-quality content that aligns with their brand personality.
Gao Yaxuan, the head of operations for celebrity authors on Douyin E-commerce, introduced that in the past year, 6.27 million creators turned their content into revenue through Douyin E-commerce. Their content creation volume increased by 252%, and total transaction amounts also more than doubled.
Behind these numbers, we can feel a thriving and vibrant author ecosystem.
Gao Yaxuan said.
Beijing Normal University's Communication Innovation and Future Media Experimental Platform previously released the "E-Commerce Industry Content Ecology Health Index (ECHI) Report," analyzing the importance of high-quality content, referred to as "new variables," in the current e-commerce industry from a data perspective. The report used the index to evaluate the content ecology situations of 27 major domestic e-commerce platforms.
According to the ranking of the e-commerce industry content ecosystem health index, Douyin E-commerce, Kuaishou, Taobao, Pinduoduo, and JD.com are ranked first to fifth.
The report believes that the e-commerce industry's content ecosystem is a comprehensive concept, integrating e-commerce with content. However, not all content can be integrated with e-commerce. High-quality carriers for integration with e-commerce are professional produced content (PGC) and user-generated content (UGC). The higher the value of the content platform, the more diverse the scenarios for consumption and promotion, and the higher the possibility of e-commerce integration, thus the stronger the commercial value. The proportion of e-commerce content production and consumption in the public and private domains will also gradually increase.
Professor Yu Guoming of the School of Journalism and Communication at Beijing Normal University, Chairman of the China Media Economics and Management Professional Committee, analyzed and interpreted the report.
He stated that, in terms of content value, the e-commerce industry has transitioned from the "accessibility of consumption" stage to the "quality-oriented consumption" stage. High-quality, professional, and differentiated content has become the "hard currency" of the e-commerce industry.
At the same time, content has become the foundation and key driver of the new stage of e-commerce development. PGC content such as knowledge payment, professional knowledge, and KOLs (key opinion leaders) has begun to become a standard feature in live streaming for e-commerce.
Looking ahead to the future development of the e-commerce industry, Yu Guoming puts forward two aspects of suggestions.
From the perspective of improving the structure of content, it aims to promote the overall improvement of the health and quality of the e-commerce content ecosystem, build positive content creation and management standards, and achieve a healthy and dynamic balance of the e-commerce industry's content ecosystem index.
Another aspect is to look at the external ecosystem; to achieve the healthy development of the content e-commerce industry and realize the value synergy and co-creation with the external environment.
The e-commerce industry in the future still needs more support in terms of data and artificial intelligence to form predictions for the stability of future development; in addition, it should provide a more standardized and healthy growth environment for merchants, achieving value synergy among enterprises, users, products, and services within the e-commerce industry, and jointly creating a healthy content ecosystem.
(End)
