This accident was classified as the most severe level 7 on the International Nuclear Event Scale (INES).
Fukushima nuclear accident caused trace amounts of radioactive substances, including iodine-131 and cesium-137 (with a half-life of 30 years), to be measured worldwide.
A large amount of radioactive isotopes were therefore released into the Pacific Ocean by the nuclear accident.
