"Fund E Account Comes: The CSRC Authorizes Development of System to Consolidate and Query All Funds Under Investor's Name - Economic Observation Network - Professional Financial News Website"
The Economic Observation Network reporter Chen Shan: Is it difficult to aggregate account information due to the complex purchasing channels of funds?
Always forgetting the "small treasury"?
The problems of the base people will soon be solved.
The China Securities Regulatory Commission (CSRC) announced on February 10th that the "Fund E Account" APP has been listed on various mobile app stores and is now launching a public trial operation.
According to the introduction, the "Fund E Account" provides a one-stop service for personal investors to query public fund accounts and share information, aiming to address the pain points of small and medium investors, such as forgetting their accounts and the cumbersome process of querying.
According to data from Wind, as of the end of 2022, there were 156 domestic fund management companies, managing a total fund scale of about 26 trillion yuan; there were 167 fund registration institutions and 411 fund sales institutions for public offering funds.
Each share registration institution's account system is independent, and there is a lack of industry-wide query channels.
Some industry professionals stated that by the end of 2021, the number of fund investors in our country exceeded 720 million, meaning that half of the population had invested in fund products.
Previously, investors had to check their purchase records through different sales institutions. With the "Fund E Account," they can query all sales channels' purchase information, making their fund holdings clearly visible.
What is the "Fund E Account" app?
The "Fund E Account" APP is a mobile application developed by China Securities Settlement Corporation, which has been approved for development by the China Securities Regulatory Commission. It serves as a one-stop portal for the public fund industry, providing investors with a comprehensive query of their holdings of off-exchange shares of public fund products across the entire market.
Investors can conveniently and efficiently manage their holdings of offshore shares of publicly offered fund products from various fund management companies through the "Fund E Account," fully enhancing the efficiency of inquiries across all sales channels in the entire market.
Specifically, investors can query the following information through the "Fund E Account": details of fund accounts opened with public fund managers across the entire market, transaction account information opened with public fund sales institutions, and holdings of off-exchange shares in products such as publicly offered securities funds and collective asset management plans managed by securities companies, which are not subject to the 200-person limit on investor numbers.
Liu Yiqian, the business director of the Shanghai Stock Exchange Fund Evaluation Research Center, told the Economic Observation Network that investors can use the "Fund E Account" app to learn about all their holdings of off-exchange public funds in one go, helping them find "forgotten assets." More importantly, it enables the comprehensive aggregation of fund investment information across all accounts for customers, helping them more timely, accurate, and comprehensively understand their investment situation, thereby better optimizing their fund portfolio and better planning their financial arrangements.
How to register and use?
The journalist noticed that the "Fund E Account" APP is now available on the app stores of Huawei, Apple, Xiaomi, OPPO, and Vivo, but the APP is still in a public trial operation phase. Registration requires an invitation code, and investors can contact the fund manager of the fund they hold to obtain it.
A customer service representative from a medium-to-large public fund in Shanghai provided a six-digit invitation code to journalists from Economic Observation Network and told them, "During the trial operation phase of the APP, China Securities Settlement provides a certain number of invitation codes to each fund manager. Investors can call to obtain them, and we will provide them."
After the trial operation is completed, users will no longer need an invitation code when opening user registration.
How are you today?
Journalists registered for the "Fund E Account" and completed inquiries according to the download and usage instructions provided on the CSRC official website. The entire process took only a few minutes and mainly consisted of four steps: user registration, real-name verification, fund account binding, and public fund inquiry.
After completing the real-name verification step, click the "Assets" fund binding button. All fund products purchased by the journalist through various fund sales platforms will be displayed in the binding options list (available accounts). After completing the binding, you can clearly see the total assets of the invested funds and start using the query functions.
It is worth noting that the "Fund E Account" only provides query services for investors and cannot be used for subscription, redemption, or trading.
The data displayed in "Fund E Account" is generally from three trading days before the date on which the user queries (T day).
For example, on February 10th, when opening the "Fund E Account", the total assets, number of fund shares, and fund net value displayed on the asset page correspond to the date three trading days prior to February 10th, i.e., February 7th.
