The worst shopping experience in history
On the evening of September 23rd, my wife's phone was dropped, and I immediately ordered an 8P on Amazon. There was stock available, but it was not from the自营 store and there was no price increase (I was secretly happy). Since it was not from the自营 store, the shipping was slower, and the system showed the latest expected delivery date was September 27th.
It's really frustrating when my wife can't use her phone. The next morning at around 6 o'clock, she called me and asked me to think of a solution. Later, when I checked Jingdong, I saw that 256G models were available and could be delivered the same day. I had no choice but to order another one immediately.
The new one has been bought, and I just wanted to cancel the Amazon order right away.
Since the order was placed in the late night, it is impossible for the courier to come to collect it in the early morning. At around 7 o'clock, the customer called the customer service to cancel the order, and the customer service replied that the order has been canceled and please wait for the SMS notification.
Well, I will wait patiently. By noon, I checked my phone and found that the order was still in the "not shipped" status. I immediately contacted customer service to request the cancellation of the order. The customer service replied that the operation was completed.
By the time it was 3 PM, I checked my phone and found the order was still there. There was no choice but to contact customer service again to clearly inform them that it was the third call. Please cancel the order and notify the seller to definitely not ship the item!
The customer service representative contacted the seller on my request and informed me that the seller is not familiar with the system and needs to become familiar with it before proceeding with the order cancellation.
But please rest assured, the seller is already aware and will definitely not ship the item.
I will check the order status on Monday, but it's already shipped, and I'm speechless.
Since we cannot contact the seller directly, we can only call the customer service again.
The subsequent handling is truly beyond comprehension, with almost everything being that I say one step and the customer service representative only follows up with a little action.
The order is still in a state of refused delivery, and we are preparing to deliver it again!
Wouldn't Amazon follow up on this actively?
The seller's company has already received the money, so it doesn't matter if they don't follow up.
Summarize that large items will never require advance payment in the future, as this is too troublesome.
